.TH SENEMOS-NABU-COLOR-PROFILE 1 "7 September 2026" "SENEMOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
senemos-nabu-color-profile \- validate and explicitly select Nabu ICC profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile catalog
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile validate
.I profile.icc
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile apply
.RB { srgb | display-p3 }
[
.BI --panel= revision
]
[
.BI --profile-dir= directory
]
[
.BI --output= connector
]
[
.B --dry-run
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile
is a native C++ runtime utility that validates packaged ICC v4 RGB profiles
and applies only an explicit user selection through KDE KScreen. It never
chooses or changes a profile automatically.
.PP
The static Android HAL sRGB and Display P3 SDR modes are supported. Native,
content-aware, PA-v2 video and HDR modes are intentionally excluded because
they cannot be represented faithfully by this conversion path.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B catalog
List supported and deliberately excluded Android modes.
.TP
.BI validate " profile.icc"
Check display class, RGB/XYZ spaces, required tags and KWin-compatible
BToA 33x33x33 LUTs.
.TP
.BI apply " profile"
Validate and apply a generated SDR profile to the enabled internal DSI output
through kscreen-doctor.
.SH SAFETY
Use
.B --dry-run
before applying a profile. Panel revision and physical color accuracy still
require device-side verification with a colorimeter. The generated profile is
an experimental conversion of the documented IGC, fine 3D LUT and GC stages,
not proof of pixel-for-pixel equivalence with Android's proprietary display
HAL.
.PP
KWin calls only EDID-derived colorimetry "Built-in". The Nabu DSI panel has no
EDID, and choosing that source would not execute the factory 3D LUT. The tool
therefore uses KWin's ICC source instead of presenting a false built-in state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/color/icc/senemos/nabu
Read-only packaged profile directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kscreen-doctor (1)
